  "repo_truth": "The worktree contains the complete uncommitted P2 planning subject at the declared 23-path fingerprint. Production, definition, schema, and test bytes in the manifest are unchanged from commit 00dde01; the resolver remains unresolved/EvidenceContractUnavailable. The planning text now declares six transaction-store failure rows and a one-review/no-repair stop rule. The parent fixture verifier reports 6 logical rows, 9 exact first-row JSON fixtures, 6 platform envelope fingerprints, and a clean git diff whitespace check. This review determines whether that planning contract is correct; it does not authorize runtime.",
  "allowed_scope": [
    "Read-only independent review of the complete declared 23-path P2 planning subject.",
    "Verify the six logical transaction-store cases form a deterministic one-to-one matrix over observation kind, five-field fingerprint/nullability tuple, store error, canonical first-row fixture, and closure-fingerprint rule.",
    "Recompute the Unix and Windows invalid-entry, alias, and 4097-entry over-limit envelopes, byte counts, SHA-256 values, and canonical first-row JSON.",
    "Verify count/alias/invalid precedence, no partial-listing behavior, and the planning-only P2S/P2A human-approval boundary.",
    "Identify findings independently, then compare only P3/P4 candidates with the selected-scope inventory."
  ],
  "non_goals": [
    "No edit, formatting, staging, commit, push, handoff, ledger write, new dispatch, or delegation.",
    "No P2 Rust, schema, definition, producer, evaluator, native adapter, CLI/compiler, Environment Context, or runtime approval.",
    "No P4 negative-proof work, P6, Phase 2 exit, HCM-3.x, another slice, or unrelated cleanup.",
    "No reuse or continuation of the exhausted prior typed review lineage; this dispatch is one new discovery cycle.",
    "No remediation loop: report any valid P1/P2 and stop."
  ],
  "tasks": [
    "Replay the manifest and confirm aggregate subject identity.",
    "Review the complete planning subject against the named authority without relying on a success assertion.",
    "Recompute and compare all platform-tagged directory-envelope fixtures, byte counts, fingerprints, row JSON, ordering, nullability, error mapping, and closure derivation.",
    "Confirm the six rows are exhaustive for the selected store failures and do not contradict scalar bounds, first-match outcome precedence, fixed transport, or no-discovery rules.",
    "Confirm coupled SPEC/plan/todo/control-pack wording grants no runtime, schema, P4, P6, Phase 2, or sibling authority.",
    "Return findings first in Critical, Required, Optional, Nit order with exact file/line, violated contract or gate, why it is wrong, smallest valid remediation, and missing verification."
  ],
  "contracts_and_gates": [
    "Exactly six named store cases: absent, unsafe, unreadable, invalid-entry, alias, and over-limit.",
    "Each case has one exact observation kind, five-field fingerprint/nullability tuple, store error, canonical first-row fixture, and closure-fingerprint rule.",
    "The first row is always the fixed evidence_transaction_store row and precedes sequence-bearing transaction observations.",
    "Retained-directory fixtures bind complete raw-name envelopes with exact platform encoding; no truncation or partial listing.",
    "The 4097-entry over-limit fixture remains within the declared 131072-byte observation bound and wins before per-name validation.",
    "No released condition or production/test/schema/definition byte changes.",
    "Planning CLEAN may permit only a reviewed planning commit and later distinct P2S/P2A human approval.",
    "A valid P1/P2 produces verdict findings and a top-level stop without remediation; P3/P4 uses exact inventory disposition."
  ],
  "stop_conditions": [
    "Return blocked if subject identity or required read-only evidence cannot be established.",
    "Report rather than repair any finding.",
    "Do not request or perform runtime/schema/P4/P6/sibling expansion.",
    "Do not create another review cycle, dispatch, handoff, ledger entry, commit, or user task hop."
  ],
